        "original_id": "046ef5e5-ac17-5418-934e-3264afb019ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edith Bouvier Beale, Edith Ewing Bouvier, Drew Barrymore, Jessica Lange, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Jacqueline Kennedy, Ken Howard, Phelan Beale, Michael Sucsy, David Levithan, Jesse Andrews\n- Films: Grey Gardens, Every Day\n- Roles: Little Edie, Big Edie\n- Topics: HBO adaptations, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Phelan Beale was born on May 23, 1881, and he was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City.\n- Phelan Beale was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, who was an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\n- Phelan Beale died on June 12, 1956.\n- Grey Gardens is an HBO film about the lives of Edith Bouvier Beale, known as Little Edie, and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier, known as Big Edie.\n- In Grey Gardens, Drew Barrymore played Little Edie and Jessica Lange played Big Edie.\n- In Grey Gardens, Jeanne Tripplehorn played Jacqueline Kennedy, who was Little Edie's cousin, and Ken Howard played Phelan Beale, who was Little Edie's father.\n- Michael Sucsy is best known for creating the HBO film Grey Gardens.\n- Every Day is an upcoming American romantic-drama directed by Michael Sucsy.\n- Every Day is based on a novel by David Levithan and was adapted by Jesse Andrews.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
